wow kim's one of the best you're lucky  to have her  she sure is we sure are seems like just  yesterday she was logging hours in dock  review  always a pleasure to see one of our  proteges spread her wings and leave the  nest  in the lead up to the final season a  better call saul there was a trend where  i saw a lot of pro howard hamlin post  pop up you saw titles like am i the only  one who thinks howard is a good guy or  howard doesn't deserve what's happening  to him everywhere as the final season  continues i see a ton of questions about  why kim and jimmy are doing what they're  doing so today i thought i would look at  their reasoning i believe there's some  interesting stuff going on here and it  might turn out to be crucial for each of  these characters endings for spoilers if  you haven't watched the first five  seasons of better call saul then this  video probably isn't for you  if the question is but why howard the  first thing to consider is what jimmy  and kim are trying to accomplish  howard's firm hhm is leading the  class-action suit against sandpiper  crossing they operate a number of  assisted living facilities across the  country and jimmy discovered that they  were ripping off their elderly clients  these types of suits take years to  settle and that means that jimmy won't  get his seven-figure payment anytime  soon sam piper has already offered to  make a settlement but as is standard hhm  and davis and maine turned it down so  they can negotiate for more kim has  decided that she wants to chase her  dream of opening a pro bono practice to  help the less fortunate get the same  representation as the wealthy and sees  jimmy's payout as a way to make this  happen right now if they can do  something to bring howard's reputation  into question that would put pressure on  the firms to settle immediately to avoid  any public relations scandals that might  make things difficult she also believes  that she can work things out and plan  things so that it will damage him but  not ruin his career of course kim and  jimmy have history with howard they both  work for him at hhm so he's the most  logical target to go after and i think  it's fair to ask the question why not  howard there's nothing particularly  noble or good about who he is he's the  face of the firm that his father started  most of what we see him do involves  keeping up appearances with clients and  eating lunch at fork there's no  indication that he's an exceptional  attorney most of hhn's reputation for  that appeared to stem from chuck's work  who also believed he was responsible for  the firm's growth and success no one  really seems to dispute that the history  is important even if the part about  jimmy comes with an asterisk in the  first episode of better call saul jimmy  learns from chuck that howard would like  him to stop using the name mcgill for  his law practice his own name this is  just one of a series of injustices which  include not hiring jimmy after he passed  a bar exam you do find out later that  chuck was behind all of this that's  where the asterisk comes in but howard  willingly went along to keep his partner  happy what's more part of his  frustration from that came out in the  way that he dealt with kim and this may  have extended to other employees kim  worked her way up through the mail room  she got help from the firm for law  school she passed the bar and then got  hired on to become one of their best up  and coming associates when she wasn't  able to convince the kettlemans to take  the very good deal she worked out for  them howard punished her by sending her  to doc review in the basement this  happens again in the second season after  the davidson main commercial incident  this seemed excessive but even though  jimmy wanted to fight back kim decided  to fix it her own way the right way she  tried to bring in a new client to get  back on the firm's good side she worked  on her own time and landed mesa verde  but howard was still reluctant to return  her to her old position eventually she  decided to leave hhm to start her own  practice and that led to a battle over  mesa verde where howard and chuck tried  their best to retain the client  so that's most of the early setup and in  the beginning of the series there was a  lot not to like about howard even though  most of the crazy stuff with jimmy was  chuck's fault where i think things start  to get interesting is after his death  particularly when kim goes to pick up  the check from chuck's estate in that  exchange she lays into howard for being  insensitive to what jimmy's going  through and this is the first time where  we see that she has something bubbling  under the surface in relation to her old  boss there's a cathartic element for her  but there's a couple of other things of  note here first is that she's protective  of her partner in a pretty fierce way  and the second is that howard sees her  point he even says what can i do to make  it right this marks the beginning of  when we start to see another side of  howard because chuck was such an  imposing character and business partner  most of what howard did was react to him  when he finally stood up and forced him  into retirement he killed himself in the  wake of that howard was saddled with  guilt but after hitting a real low point  he was able to turn things around in  that time he became sympathetic so when  at the end of season 5 kim brings up her  plan even jimmy doesn't think he  deserves what she has in mind i think  the timing of things explains a lot and  his approaching her at the courthouse in  the season 5 finale is the event that  set things into motion the exchange  highlights a lot of what's going on i  guess before i go through the ways that  set kim off i should mention that it  also works to keep howard likeable since  he's coming from a place of genuine  concern for jimmy he believes he needs  help based on the bowling ball and  prostitutes showing up at lunch  incidents and the lightning bolts shoot  from my fingertips tirade at the  courthouse how he approaches kim is  where he goes wrong he not only implies  that she doesn't know what's going on  with her partner but that he must be  manipulating her because her decision to  walk away from schweikert and coakley  doesn't make sense to him so he  questions her ability to make her own  decisions and he activated her sense of  wanting to protect jimmy even if what  he's saying about him is true kim knows  him and doesn't feel like she needs  howard to swoop in and help to explain  what's going on and i mentioned the  timing this is immediately after his  trip to the desert they're still hiding  out at the hotel and when she goes back  there jimmy suggests that maybe they  should just go home she can see that  he's not out of the woods as far as his  ptsd and you see her shift into this  space where she's trying to figure out  how to make him feel better throughout  the series we've seen that pulling a con  is something that brings them closer  together and i think that plays a part  in her coming up with this idea as they  eat and talk she brings it up and  notices that it gets his attention plus  it's justifiable if they can pull it off  they'll get the money for the pro bono  practice in her mind that would help a  lot of people she can get back at howard  for personal reasons and she can maybe  bring jimmy back from this dark place  he's in it starts to work and they come  together and by the time jimmy tries to  pull back kim just takes that as a cue  that she'll need to take charge she does  that and that's pretty much how things  got started i think there's more to it  that will come out in the next handful  of episodes to me it seems like there's  something from her past that makes her  resent people like howard where he came  from and the world they inhabit together  we've had a few glimpses into her past  and know that she worked really hard to  get to where she's at i feel like even  in her accomplishments there was a sense  of disappointment there that's popped up  over the past few seasons she threw  herself into the pro bono work trying to  make the other stuff make sense and when  that didn't work she decided to walk  away completely i do think that howard  works as a symbol of all of what she  finds distasteful about this situation  his story is basically the polar  opposite of hers and that's why she's  more motivated to take him down than  jimmy is  i think the scene where she cuts him to  check for her tuition after running into  him at lunch is a great example of that  coming out and i don't think the  connection kim and jimmy have as  outsiders in that world should be  overlooked either  to wrap things up it's not weird to like  howard and not want him to get destroyed  at this stage in the game he started out  unlikable and in my opinion is still not  remarkable but patrick fabian does sell  the performance also the writers started  to make him sympathetic at the same time  the other characters were starting to do  awful things that weren't as easy to  overlook in some ways he looks great i  suppose at this point i'd feel bad if  something happens to him but i'm still  rooting for kim and jimmy because that's  how i am and i think that's a good place  to leave things let me know in the  comments what you think about howard how  we got to where we are and how this plan  is going to go down please like this  video if you enjoyed it please subscribe  to my channel if you haven't already and  thanks for watching i'll talk to you  soon

